{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1510,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You've probably seen footage of the Tacoma\nnarrows bridge collapse in 1940 (if not, it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5930,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all over the internet)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7450,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while I've heard that in Seattle they\njust call it bad bridge building, most teachers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11190,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and physics textbooks have probably told you\nthat the bridge collapsed because of resonance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15190,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the wind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16300,
    "dDurationMs": 1239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they're wrong!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17539,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because a resonance is a vibration\ndriven by a source oscillating at a similar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21000,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frequency - like how a swing at the park goes\nhigher and higher as you push it, or the electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25490,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in an antenna move in tandem with the electromagnetic\nwaves of a radio signal, or how a guitar string"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30210,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vibrates or wine glass shatters if you sing\nat just the right pitch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34370,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's not what happened at the Tacoma\nnarrows, because people at the bridge that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37620,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day measured the windspeed as being fairly\nconstant, or, 'not-oscillating.'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there was no forced resonance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44440,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's also tempting to think that the bridge\ncollapsed because of vortex shedding, a cool-looking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48149,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fluid process where vortices take turns sloughing\noff of the edge of an object - but that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52100,
    "dDurationMs": 1099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not right either."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53199,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What did cause the bridge to collapse is a\nphenomenon called aeroelastic flutter – the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57079,
    "dDurationMs": 3701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same thing that causes a strip of paper or\nblade of grass to vibrate if you hold it tight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60780,
    "dDurationMs": 1649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and blow straight at the edge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62429,
    "dDurationMs": 4641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically, with enough wind speed, the bridge\nstarted to twist a little bit - but then gravity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67070,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tension in the bridge caused it to twist\nback down, except too far!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70720,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now the wind could push it in the opposite\ndirection, causing it to twist more violently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74830,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so on and so forth until, well… the\nbridge fluttered itself into destruction!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And aeroelastic flutter isn't just limited\nto bridges - it can cause airplane wings to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84120,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hum annoyingly, or vibrate so vigorously as\nto disintegrate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87210,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But don't worry - the last time this happened\non a commercial airplane was in the early"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91030,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1960s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92360,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You should probably be more concerned with\nthe haunted swingset in Firmat, Argentina"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96000,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can swing on its own for days - oh wait,\nno, that's just aeroelastic flutter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100170,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sorry ghosts - physics just blew you away."
    } ]
  } ]
}
